====================================================================================================
Z09 -- THE UFD KINEMATIC FALSIFIER: the never-froze class predicted beta ~ 0
====================================================================================================
  freeze floor sigma_min = 65.0 km/s @ 5 keV (z* = 0); T_b = m sigma^2/k_B; z* = T_b/T_CMB(0) - 1
  frozen reference (G209 E1 committed): beta 0.033/0.093/0.173/0.305/0.560 at 0.5-1/1-1.5/1.5-2/2-3/3-5 R500; galaxy envelope 0.565 at 2-4 r_M (G218)
  n = 34 measured dSphs (G070 compendium, committed); distances from Simon 2019 Table 1 (dwarf_tab.tex, committed source)

====================================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE PREDICTION AND THE FALSIFIER: the N per radial bin for a
3-sigma beta detection vs the isotropic null in the never-froze class
====================================================================================================

  THE FROZEN REFERENCE (G209 E1, committed): beta = 0.033 / 0.093 / 0.173 / 0.305 / 0.560 at 0.5-1 / 1-1.5 / 1.5-2 / 2-3 / 3-5 R500 (rising 0.03 -> 0.56); galaxy envelope beta = 0.565 at 2-4 r_M (G218).
  THE PREDICTION: the never-froze class (z* < 0, T_b < T_CMB(0), sigma_v 2-11 km/s < sigma_min = 65.0 km/s) has NOT had time to develop the streaming envelope: beta(r) ~ 0 at ALL radii.

  THE ESTIMATOR: beta_B = 1 - <v_t^2>/(2 <v_los^2>); at the null
  SE(beta) = sqrt([(s_t^2)^2 + 2 (s_l^2)^2]/[(N-1)(s_l^2)^2]), s^2 = sigma_v^2 + e^2.
  N_req = 1 + 9 [(s_t^2)^2 + 2 (s_l^2)^2] / [beta_c^2 (s_l^2)^2]  (3 sigma, per radial bin).

