  DISTANCE EFFECT ON THE PM ERROR AXIS (the decision variable):
    1 mas/yr = 4.74057 x D(kpc) km/s: at 30 kpc, 142 km/s; at 50 kpc, 237 km/s; at 100 kpc, 474 km/s.  The internal PM signal of the UFD class is sigma_v/(4.74 D): 5 km/s @ 50 kpc = 0.021 mas/yr -- BELOW the Gaia DR3 single-star errors (0.05-0.3 mas/yr at G 19-21); the HSTPROMO per-star PM errors (multi-epoch) are quoted BELOW the intrinsic dispersion -> e_t ~ 2-5 km/s at 50-100 kpc.

====================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE INTERMEDIATE CLASS AND THE PREDICTED ORDERING
====================================================================================================

  THE FREEZE FLOOR: sigma_min = 65.0 km/s @ 5 keV (z* = 0).  THE DSPH CLASS'S REACH: sigma_pred in [1.07, 17.79] km/s -- max = 17.8 (Sagittarius) is a factor 3.7 SHORT of the floor: the z* ~ 0 intermediate bin is UNPOPULATED in the dwarf spheroidal class (the systems with sigma_pred ~ 40-80 km/s do not exist in the dSph catalog -- the next rung up is the gas-rich/irregular class, not quasi-spherical equilibria).

  THE PREDICTED ORDERING (beta amplitude vs z* across the dwarf class):
    z* ~ -0.999  (UFDs, sigma_pred 1-3):      beta ~ 0   (never-froze, isotropy)
    z* ~ -0.90   (bright dSphs, 6-17 km/s):   partial envelope -> small POSITIVE, rising from 0
    z* ~ 0       (the floor, sigma_pred ~ 65): the FIRST full envelope -- UNOBSERVED class
    z* = +2.4    (galaxy class, 119 km/s):    beta = 0.565 at 2-4 r_M (G218)
    z* = 84-232  (cluster class, 600-992):    beta 0.03 -> 0.56 profile (G209)

  THE MEASURED POINTS (UNVERIFIED):
    Draco     z*(pred) = -0.991  r_M = 26 pc, data to 900 pc = ~34 r_M  -> beta_bar_B = -0.20 +0.28/-0.53  (z vs 0 = 0.7 sigma)
    Sculptor  z*(pred) = -0.978  r_M = 64 pc, PM data 120-240 pc = 2-4 r_M     -> beta ~ -0.16 +- 0.13 (DERIVED; authors: consistent with isotropy)
  THE ORDERING TEST ON EXISTING DATA: at radii where the FROZEN class shows beta = 0.31-0.56, the measured never-froze points show beta ~ 0 -- both on the predicted side; n = 2 points -> no correlation statistic yet, the ordering table's first rows populated, direction consistent.
  THE FRAMEWORK-INTERNAL AXIS (already measured on the committed data): the excess E = |log10(pred/obs)| vs z*(sigma_pred, 5 keV): Spearman rho = -0.691, p = 6.1e-6 (G213 registered) -- the deeper below the freeze floor, the larger the departure (the more unfrozen).  The predicted kinematic twin: beta ~ -E (more unfrozen -> smaller beta).  Executable once PM-based betas land for the UFD class: the SAME objects that sit above the equipartition line (E > 0) should sit at beta ~ 0.
    [recomputed on the committed CSVs] rho(E, z*_pred) = -0.691, p = 6.13e-06  (G213's -0.691 / 6.1e-6 reproduced: OK)
  [PASS] C0 [the never-froze class] every measured dSph has z* < 0 (z*(pred) in [-0.9997, -0.9251], z*(obs) in [-0.9987, -0.9676] @ 5 keV) -- the whole class sits below the freeze floor, the domain of the beta ~ 0 prediction
         measured: z*(pred) max = -0.9251 < 0; n = 34
         reading : G213 C4's committed result reproduced on the same CSV

